$DIR/main.p:22:14: cannot use "not a number" (untyped string constant) as int value in variable declaration
    n is declared as int, so it can only hold whole numbers; "not a number"
    holds text. Plutonium, like Go, never converts between text and numbers
    automatically.
    (see "Assignability" in the Plutonium spec, section 8.4)
    (run "pluto explain E0023" for a longer explanation)
